CD [drive]
  This slot's drive. CD alone: the drive (and its path), the drives with
  paths and the devices. B: alone on the command line is CD B.
UniDOS - a drive letter can be a path (a device's folder):
  CD IDE:  CD IDE  IDE:      a device: this drive's path (from A, B or a RAM
                             disc: the first free letter from C gets it)
  CD SD:GAMES/ACTION         a device's folder
  CD GAMES   CD ..           a folder here; the folder this one is in
  CD C: IDE:WORK             drive C's path set, C this slot's drive
  CD C: -                    drive C's path dropped
  CD DFA:  CD DFB:           a floppy (FLOPPY A lists its files)
  A folder named as a device: CD SD/. A RAM disc's letter has no path.
  C: --> IDE:  means drive C goes to IDE:.
